  "findings": "Compared the Oregon State habitat and leaf photographs with revised small, medium and large pilots and all 36 variants. Reduced broad generic leaves to fine 45 mm leaf envelopes and added fine terminal forks and green young stems. The open angular shrub now shows real branch-following foliage and irregular gaps; heights span 1.18-2.58 m. Leaf envelopes mildly exaggerate the botanical 10-30 mm blades to survive 25 mm sampling; red twig gradients and translucent leaves await the separate approved appearance work. No summer berries. Accepted as a stylized spring red huckleberry source; variants remain pending user endorsement.",
